"Language: es-419\n"

#. Button on the END OF SLICE card. Starts a fresh run. All caps in English by design.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:243 PLAY_AGAIN_TEXT
msgid "PLAY AGAIN"
msgstr "JUGAR DE NUEVO"

#. Title-screen note when Continue has nothing to load. SAFE POINT is the in-world name of the save station (glossary term).
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:184 NO_CHECKPOINT_NOTE
msgid "No checkpoint yet. Saving starts at the first SAFE POINT."
msgstr "Aún no hay punto de control. Se empieza a guardar en el primer PUNTO SEGURO."

#. Context hint above the dialogue bar while the engineer cranks the manual bypass. 'E' is the bound key (rebindable; the key name is swapped in by code later). The two %d are turns done and turns needed, in that order.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:176 BYPASS_HOLD_OFFER_HINT
msgid "HOLD E: crank on, %d of %d, or let WOLF take the relay."
msgstr "MANTÉN E: sigue girando, %d de %d, o deja que WOLF se encargue del relé."

#. Fail card after the sentry runs the engineer down. %s is the engineer's first name (Rowan, Alex or Morgan; any gender). TANK RELEASE is the station label the player can see (glossary term, must match L10). The line break is authored.
#: apps/game/scripts/junction_room.gd:401 SENTRY_REASON
msgid "The sentry saw %s out in the open.\nStay close to the TANK RELEASE."
msgstr "El centinela vio a %s al descubierto.\nQuédate junto a SOLTAR TANQUE."

#. Narration box when the engineer first pulls the manual bypass handle. Present tense, terse, physical.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:169 BYPASS_START_LINE
msgid "The bypass handle is stiff. Coolant hisses from the relay housing and an alarm starts to wail."
msgstr "La palanca del bypass está dura. Sale refrigerante silbando de la carcasa del relé y una alarma empieza a aullar."

#. Opening cinematic caption. WOLF (a robotic wolf, he/him) wakes up on his own, without an order. The line break is authored.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:198 opening beat 3
msgid "Nobody gives an activation command.\nWOLF wakes himself."
msgstr "Nadie da una orden de activación.\nWOLF se despierta por sí mismo."

#. WOLF speaks to the engineer at the breaker. 'his' is the Director. 'WOLF: ' is the speaker tag the dialogue splitter reads; it is not translated.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:163 STAKES_LINE
msgid "WOLF: That purge takes the original program logs. Once they're gone, his word is the only record."
msgstr "WOLF: Esa purga se lleva los registros originales del programa. Cuando ya no estén, su palabra será el único registro."

#. WOLF refuses to lure the sentry because the engineer rushed him earlier at the relay. Calm, direct, not sulking. 'it' is the sentry; 'the release' is the TANK RELEASE station; 'the mark' is the floor spot under the tank.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:269 BAIT_NO_LINE
msgid "WOLF: At the relay you'd have sent me in blind. I won't walk into its sights. Time the drop from the release; it crosses the mark on every pass."
msgstr "WOLF: En el relé me habrías mandado a ciegas. No voy a meterme en su mira. Elige cuándo soltar desde el control; pasa por la marca en cada vuelta."

#. End-card recap row. 'SENTRY' is the row's topic label, two spaces, then the summary. {name} is the engineer's first name (any gender; they/them in English). 'alone' must not reveal a gender.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:236 RECAP_LANE_REFUSED
msgid "SENTRY  WOLF wouldn't draw it, so {name} timed the drop alone."
msgstr "CENTINELA  WOLF no quiso atraerlo, así que {name} calculó la caída sin ayuda."

#. Station plate over the lever that drops a coolant tank. 12 px caps on a small plate; must match the term used in L04.
#: apps/game/scripts/junction_room.gd:793
msgid "TANK RELEASE"
msgstr "SOLTAR TANQUE"

#. Answer button: the ENGINEER says this to WOLF, telling him the risk and letting him decide. Second person addresses WOLF.
#: apps/game/scripts/m0_state.gd:21 disclose_risk
msgid "The relay may vent coolant. Your call."
msgstr "El relé podría soltar refrigerante. Tú decides."

#. Narration after the sealed door blows. %s is the engineer's first name; the possessive must work with any name. The line break is authored.
#: apps/game/scripts/main.gd:256 RUBBLE_LINE
msgid "The door goes. WOLF falls back\nto wait for %s's call."
msgstr "La puerta cede. WOLF retrocede\npara esperar la señal de %s."
